# File-Based Pages (`src/pages/`)

Routes are **not registered manually**. The `octane-pages` Vite plugin scans `src/pages/` at dev/build time and generates:

- `src/pages/.generated/routes.ts` — `matchRoute()`, path matching
- `src/pages/.generated/PageRouter.tsrx` — renders the active page or `404.tsrx`

Run `npm run generate:pages` after clone (also runs before `typecheck`). Generated output is gitignored.

## File naming (TanStack Start style)

All route **filenames and folder names must be lowercase**.

| File | URL |
| --- | --- |
| `index.tsrx` | `/` |
| `about.tsrx` | `/about` |
| `posts/index.tsrx` | `/posts` |
| `posts/$post_id.tsrx` | `/posts/:post_id` |
| `docs/$.tsrx` | `/docs/*` (splat → `params._splat`) |
| `404.tsrx` | Not a route — global not-found page |

- **`index`** — index route for the parent path
- **`$param`** — dynamic segment (available as `matchRoute(path)?.params.param`)
- **`[segment]`** — literal segment (escape special names)
- Files/folders starting with `_` or `.` are ignored

## Optional language prefix — `(lang)/`

Place pages inside `(lang)/` to match **with and without** a language prefix:

| File | URLs | `params.lang` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `(lang)/artikel.tsrx` | `/artikel`, `/de/artikel`, `/en/artikel` | set only on prefixed URL |

For a **required** prefix only, use `$lang/artikel.tsrx` → `/de/artikel`, `/en/artikel` (no unprefixed URL).

## Wiring

```
RouterContext (path, navigate)
    ↓
PageContent → PageRouter (.generated)
    ↓
matchRoute(path) → page component or 404.tsrx
```

- Internal links: `useRouter().navigate('/about')` — no full reloads
- Route params: `import { matchRoute } from '../.generated/routes.ts'`
- Document language: `RouterContext` sets `document.documentElement.lang` via `resolveRouteLanguage()` (`params.lang` or `DEFAULT_LANG` from `.env`)
- Every page receives a **`language` prop** from `PageRouter` — type as `PageProps` from `src/pages/types.ts`

## Page file rules (TSRX)

- One exported page component per file; use a **unique export name** per file (codegen aliases by file path, but duplicate names are confusing)
- Use `@{ ... }` with a **single JSX root** — never `return <Component />` inside `@{}`
- Accept `PageProps` (`language: string`) on exported page components — passed by generated `PageRouter`
- Async data with `use(promise)` requires a `<Suspense>` boundary (see `src/pages/articles/$article_id.tsrx`)
- Compose shared UI from `src/components/`; keep pages thin

## Do

- Add new routes by creating lowercase `.tsrx` files under `src/pages/`
- Prefer `(lang)/` for localized URLs that also work without a prefix
- Check `match.id` or specific `params` when a component could be ambiguous across routes

## Don't

- Edit `src/pages/.generated/` by hand
- Hardcode route registries or template switches
- Use uppercase filenames (`About.tsrx` → use `about.tsrx`)
- Put `404.tsrx` on a URL path — it is only the fallback component
